name: sim.getObjectPosition
description: Retrieves the position of an object
luaSynopsis: list position = sim.getObjectPosition(int objectHandle, int relativeToObjectHandle = sim.handle_world)
pythonSynopsis: float[3] position = sim.getObjectPosition(int objectHandle, int relativeToObjectHandle = sim.handle_world)
inputs:
1. objectHandle: handle of the object. Can be combined with sim.handleflag_reljointbaseframe (see next argument)
2. relativeToObjectHandle: indicates relative to which reference frame we want the position. Specify sim.handle_world to retrieve the absolute position, sim.handle_parent to retrieve the position relative to the object's parent, or an object handle relative to whose reference frame we want the position. If this handle is the handle of a joint, then the position relative to the joint's moving frame will be returned (unless objectHandle is combined with sim.handleflag_reljointbaseframe, in which case the position relative to the joint's base frame will be returned).
outputs:
1. position: array of 3 values [x y z]
replacedBy:
- name: getPosition, class: sceneObject, file: sceneObject_getPosition.method
- name: position, class: sceneObject, file: sceneObject_position.property
- name: worldPosition, class: sceneObject, file: sceneObject_worldPosition.property
